; NDPARTA.DSF - SP11 Task 6 two-part fixture, part A (game root).
; Paired with NDPARTB.DSF (part 2, staged as GAME2.DDB + PART2\0.XMB).
; Proves the EXTERN n 4 (XPART) switch primitive, the cross-part LOAD
; and RAMLOAD auto-switch primitives (h_load/h_ramload's own part-
; mismatch -> xpart_load_entry -> switch_to_part wiring), part-to-part
; flag and object carry, and the PARTn\ asset probe (via each part's
; own 0.XMB) end to end. Not part of the automated condacts.dsf suite -
; staged and run separately via tests\build-tests.ps1 -Part. Cannot be
; exercised by the implementing agent (no CSpect/emulator access) -
; this is the owner's leg.
;
; Owner leg - exact commands:
;   ./tests/build-tests.ps1 -Part
;   ./build.ps1 -Run
;
; Four switches happen in this run, both directions of both switch
; mechanisms: EXTERN forward (A->B), EXTERN back (B->A), LOAD forward
; auto-switch (A->B, triggered by loading a save whose stored part
; differs from the running one), RAMLOAD back auto-switch (B->A, same
; idea via the RAM buffer). Flag 103 is the discriminator that lets
; PRO 0 tell every re-entry apart: 0 on a genuine cold boot and on the
; RAMLOAD-restored return (the RAMSAVE below is taken BEFORE part B
; ever sets 103, and is never refreshed again), 1 on the EXTERN-return
; and the LOAD-restored re-entry (both carry a state where part B has
; already set it).
;
; Expected screen output, in order:
;   PA BOOT
;   (part one external text via XMESSAGE - informational only)
;   [switch to part 2 - no visible marker on success]
;   PB CARRY OK
;   part two external text via PART2        <- must read EXACTLY this
;   PB TYPE NAME: pt    <- type any 1-8 char name (e.g. pt), press ENTER
;   PB TYPE NAME: pt    <- type the SAME name again, press ENTER
;   PB SAV OK
;   [switch back to part 1 - no visible marker on success]
;   PA RETURN OK
;   PA TYPE NAME: pt    <- type the SAME name a THIRD time, press ENTER
;   [LOAD auto-switches forward to part 2 - no visible marker on success]
;   PB XLOAD OK
;   [RAMLOAD auto-switches back to part 1 - no visible marker on success]
;   PA RAMLOAD OK
;   "Would you like another go?" (SM13) - Y or N ends the leg either way
;
; One SAVE and two LOADs share the same on-disk file (SAVE/LOAD names
; live in one namespace in the game root regardless of part), so all
; three prompts above must be answered with the SAME typed name.
;
; Any line ending " F" (PA SWITCH F, PB CARRY F, PB SAV F, PB SWITCH F,
; PA XLOAD F, PB XLOAD F, PB RAMLOAD F) is a defect. Anything other
; than the exact clean sentence where "part two external text via
; PART2" belongs - garbled characters or a different sentence entirely
; - is a defect. The sequence stalling or looping (repeating any line)
; is also a defect - stop and report it, do not continue.
;
; Optional title variant: ./tests/build-tests.ps1 -Part -Title (the two
; staging blocks are independent, so combined staging works) then
; ./build.ps1 -Run. The title screen must appear once at cold boot only
; - never again at any of the four switches, since a switch jumps
; straight into the new part's PRO 0 and never revisits the boot/title
; chain.
;
; NOTE: no CLS anywhere in this fixture's PRO 0 (a deliberate departure
; from condacts.dsf's own opening-CLS idiom) - the whole point of this
; leg is a human-readable transcript of every line above, in order, on
; one screen; clearing partway through would hide the evidence.

/CTL
_

/VOC
